{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>יכפרנה</b> — He nullifies it, and his wrath turns away of itself. And the explanation of \"he will lighten his eyes upon the wise\": there is life, and his will is that he favor him like the latter rain that causes the after-growth to sprout. And the acquisition of wisdom — how good it is for the wise, for it nullifies the king's wrath." "<b>חרוץ</b> — from the root גזור (to decree), as in אתה חרצת (you have decreed), or it is a name of gold, like כתם (refined gold)."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:10.183711910Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}